| **Compaction absorb** | **Accepted**, mitigated by nudging the compaction prompt to scope its preferences section to the current conversation |\n| Namespace | `user.chats.*`, not `user.personalization.*` |\n| Eval | Skipped; #307's Acceptance rewritten |\n| Untitled | Omit — title arrival is the eligibility gate |\n| Archived / current chat | Both excluded |\n| Pins filter | `item_type = 'chat'` |\n| Public/shared path | Absent, fail-closed |\n| Receipt | Free via the snapshot |\n| Toggle-off / chat deletion | Both non-retroactive; both stated spec limitations |\n| Delta content | Same shape as baseline, excerpts included (taken on my recommendation) |\n| Parallel issues | #327 `recent_chats` tool · #328 pin ordering |\n\n### Open\n\n**1. Re-bake policy** — the question above. Never / at compaction / at compaction + model switch. My rec: the third.\n\n**2. Delta cap** — moot if you take re-baking (resets per epoch). Live if you don't: needs a ceiling, ~20 cumulative.\n\n**3. One setting or two** — still unanswered, and now spans three issues. #307's digest toggle, #326's `search_conversations` gate, #327's tool gate. You said #327 rides \"the same switch\" but not which. One setting across all three is coherent (\"share my chat history with the assistant\"); two is defensible (injection vs. retrieval are different consent acts). Schema call, expensive to unwind, cheap to decide now.\n\n**4. Model-switch orphaning** — dissolved by re-bake option 3; otherwise needs a mechanism where an omitted block suppresses deltas.\n\nThat's four, and 2 and 4 both collapse into 1. So realistically: **the re-bake policy and the settings question.** Answer those two and I'll write the proposal — `chat-recency-digest` capability spec, `model-system-prompts` delta for `each`, `personalization` delta for the toggle, and the #307 rewrite.",
