ign decisions\n\n- **Deltas are derived by set difference, never timestamps.** Nothing records when a title landed, and unpinning is a hard row delete — a timestamp-based derivation is blind to two of three transitions. The diff is asymmetric, so displacement, archival, and deletion need no rules of their own.\n- **Pin state means membership in `pins`, never in the rendered list.** Otherwise every cap displacement fabricates an unpin.\n- **Re-bake at compaction only.** A model switch re-renders the same frozen baseline — compaction is a context boundary, a switch is only a provider boundary.\n- **Top-level `chats` context, not `user.chats`.** Nesting under `user` would make `{{#if user}}` true for an owner with chats but no personalization, breaking a shipped `personalization` scenario.\n- **`model-system-prompts` gains bounded `each`** over declared collections, with a cross-product boot probe.\n\n## Accepted, not solved\n\nDocumented as risks rather than quietly resolved: conversation-derived text acquiring system-role authority; enabling reaching backwards over the whole corpus while disabling does not reach forwards; chat deletion not reaching already-bound prompts; unbounded appends in chats that never compact; and a snapshot table that grows per chat rather than per owner.\n\n## Review provenance\n\nThree rounds of paired adversarial review plus a targeted propagation sweep — 29 findings, every load-bearing one verified against the repository before applying. Two rounds caught contradictions that would have produced wrong implementations (mutually exclusive requirements about the disabled setting; an optimization that made its own normative scenario unreachable). `design.md` carries the v1→v6 revision history.\n\n## Stack\n\n```\n(master) <- recency-digest/spec   <- this PR\n         <- recency-digest/templating\n         <- recency-digest/settings\n         <- recency-digest/baseline\n         <- recency-digest/deltas\n         <- recency-digest/compaction\n 