            "content": "# Lane: `recency-digest/templating` (layer 1 of 7)\n\nYou are a builder. Implement ONE layer of an already-designed, already-reviewed change.\nThe design is settled — implement it, do not redesign it.\n\n## Absolute rules\n\n- **NEVER run any `git` command.** No commit, no stash, no checkout, no reset, no branch.\n  The orchestrating session owns all version control. Editing files is your entire job.\n  A `git stash` here destroys in-progress work that is not yours.\n- **Touch ONLY the files in the declared file set below.** Writing outside it fails the lane.\n- Do not create scratch/summary/plan markdown files in the repo.\n\n## Repo\n\n`/home/leon0399/.herdr/worktrees/llame/recent-chats-digest-in-prompt` — pnpm + Turborepo,\nTypeScript end-to-end, NestJS API in `apps/api`. Read `apps/api/AGENTS.md` before editing;\nit is authoritative on conventions.\n\n## Normative sources — READ THESE FIRST\n\n1. `openspec/changes/add-chat-recency-digest/specs/model-system-prompts/spec.md`\n   — the normative requirement text for this layer. Every SHALL is binding.\n2. `openspec/changes/add-chat-recency-digest/tasks.md` section `## 1. recency-digest/templating`\n   — tasks 1.0 through 1.10, which are your definition of done.\n3. `openspec/changes/add-chat-recency-digest/design.md` — decisions D5 (top-level `chats`),\n   D6 (bounded `each`), D12 (reserved delimiter).\n4. `apps/api/AGENTS.md` — the \"Prompt files are Handlebars templates\" section.\n\n## What this layer does, and what it deliberately does NOT do\n\nThis layer teaches the prompt template validator/renderer a new **bounded iteration**\nconstruct and a new **top-level `chats` context**, so a later layer can render a chat\nrecency digest. It ships **no digest data, no database, no settings, and no change to the\npackaged default prompt**. Nothing about it is user-observable. It is pure capability\nin the templating surface plus its tests.\n\nDo NOT add: DB schema, migrations, HTTP endpoints, a digest resolver, or a digest block in\n`apps/api/src/prompts/chat-default.md`. Those are later layers and adding them fails this lane.\n\n## Declared file set — you may touch these and nothing else\n\n- `apps/api/src/instance-config/prompt-loader.ts` (primary)\n- `apps/api/src/instance-config/prompt-loader.test.ts`\n- `apps/api/src/instance-config/authored-text.ts`\n- `apps/api/src/instance-config/authored-text.test.ts`\n- `apps/api/src/models/model-catalog.ts` (add the input type beside `PromptUserInput`)\n- `apps/api/src/system-prompts/system-prompts.service.ts` (thread the new optional arg)\n- `apps/web/lib/services/personalization/sanitize.ts` (mirror the reserved name)\n- `apps/web/lib/services/personalization/sanitize.test.ts`\n- `apps/api/AGENTS.md` (task 1.10 documentation)\n\nIf you believe a file outside this set must change, STOP and say so in your final message\ninstead of editing it.\n\n## Architecture decisions (settled — implement these, do not relitigate)\n\n### 1. Context shape\n\nAdd beside `PromptUserInput` in `apps/api/src/models/model-catalog.ts`:\n\n```ts\nexport type PromptChatDigestEntry = {\n  title: string;\n  /** Last-activity date, preformatted by the caller. */\n  date: string;\n  messageCount: number;\n  excerpt?: string | null;\n};\n\nexport type PromptChatsInput = {\n  pinned?: readonly PromptChatDigestEntry[];\n  recent?: readonly PromptChatDigestEntry[];\n  pinnedShown: number;\n  pinnedTotal: number;\n  recentShown: number;\n  recentTotal: number;\n  /** Date the digest was compiled, preformatted by the caller. */\n  compiledOn: string;\n};\n```\n\n`renderSystemPromptTemplate(template, model, user?, chats?)` takes it as a 4th optional\nparameter; `SystemPromptsService.render(model, user?, chats?)` threads it through.\nNo caller supplies it yet — that is correct for this layer.\n\n### 2. Declared collections and their item fields\n\nDeclare a single source of truth mapping collection path -> its declared item field names:\n`chats.pinned` and `chats.recent`, each declaring exactly `title`, `date`, `messageCount`,\n`excerpt`. Follow the existing style: a module-level constant beside `PROMPT_CONTEXT_PATHS`,\nkeyed with the same `toContextKey` `\\0`-join trick so a bracketed path cannot spoof it.\nLater capabilities extend the constant, not the validator.\n\n### 3. Path positions — there are now FOUR, not two\n\n| Path | value position | conditional subject | `each` subject | inside `each` body |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `model.*`, `user.*` leaf paths | allowed | allowed | **rejected** | rejected |\n| `user`, `user.personalization` | rejected | allowed | **rejected** | rejected |\n| `chats` | rejected | **allowed** | **rejected** | rejected |\n| `chats.pinned`, `chats.recent` | **rejected** | **allowed** | **allowed** | rejected |\n| `chats.pinnedShown` / `pinnedTotal` / `recentShown` / `recentTotal` / `compiledOn` | **allowed** | allowed | **rejected** | rejected |\n| `title` / `date` / `messageCount` / `excerpt` | rejected | rejected | rejected | **allowed** (value AND conditional) |\n\n`{{#if excerpt}}` inside an `each` body must work — `excerpt` is genuinely optional, so\ngating on it is the whole point. `{{#if chats.recent}}` must work. `{{chats.recent}}` must\nfail boot exactly the way `{{user}}` does.\n\n### 4. `each` validation rules (all of these fail boot naming the construct)\n\n- exactly one parameter, and it must be a declared collection path\n- `each` over a scalar (including the five metadata scalars), a gate-only path, or an\n  unknown path\n- an `each` nested inside another `each`\n- block parameters (`as |chat|`)\n- `@index`, `@key`, `@first`, `@last`, or any `@`-data reference inside the body\n- a hash argument on `each`\n- a path with `depth > 0` (`../`) anywhere\n- inside an `each` body, any path that is not one of that collection's declared item fields\n\nImplement this by threading an **item scope** through `assertStatements`/`assertPath`:\nwhen inside an `each`, the permitted path set is exactly that collection's item fields\n(single-segment paths only), and the outer allowlists are NOT reachable. When outside,\nitem fields are NOT reachable. The `@`-data check matters: handlebars parses `@index` as a\n`PathExpression` with `data: true`, which the current segment-based check would not catch.\n\n### 5. Render-context projection and omission\n\nProject `chats` at the **TOP LEVEL**, never under `user`. This is load-bearing, not\nstylistic: nesting it under `user` would make `{{#if user}}` true for an owner who has\nchats but authored no personalization, rendering an operator's personalization framing\nprose around no content. There is a required test for exactly this (task 1.9).\n\nOmission mirrors the existing three-level `userContext` discipline:\n- an entry's `excerpt` with no value is omitted from that entry\n- a collection that is empty or absent is omitted entirely (never an empty array — an\n  empty array is truthy, so `{{#if chats.recent}}` would wrongly pass)\n- `chats` itself is omitted when **neither collection** would render — including its\n  metadata scalars, which have no meaning with nothing listed\n\n### 6. Neutralization split\n\n- The five metadata scalars: `escapeForPrompt` (the strict `&<>` escape), like model and\n  account-identity values. They are server-computed numbers and dates.\n- **All four item fields** (`title`, `date`, `messageCount`, `excerpt`): `sanitizeAuthoredText`,\n  the tag-balance sanitizer. The spec is explicit that rendered digest item values take the\n  two tag rules. `messageCount` is stringified first.\n\nReuse the existing `promptValue(raw, neutralize)` helper — it already encodes the\nabsent/empty/trim omission rule and returns a `SafeString` from the created environment.\nDo NOT patch `Handlebars.Utils.escapeExpression`; the file comment explains why\n(`Handlebars.create()` shares `Utils` by reference process-wide).\n\n### 7. Reserved delimiter\n\nAdd `user_chat_history` to `RESERVED_TAG_NAMES` in `apps/api/src/instance-config/authored-text.ts`\nand to the byte-mirrored copy in `apps/web/lib/services/personalization/sanitize.ts`.\nKeep the two files in sync — that mirroring is an existing documented invariant.\nThe reservation must land in THIS layer, before any layer renders digest values.\n\n### 8. Cross-product boot probe\n\nThe boot probe in `createModelPromptLoader().resolve()` currently renders twice, varying\nonly the per-user context. It must now render the **cross product** of the `user` and\n`chats` gates — all four combinations of (absent, populated) x (absent, populated).\n\nVarying them in lockstep is unsound and there is a required test for it: a template whose\nwhole body sits inside `{{#if user}}{{#unless chats}}...{{/unless}}{{/if}}` renders\nnon-empty when both are absent and when both are populated, yet renders **empty** for\nexactly the owners who have chats but no personalization. A lockstep probe passes it at\nboot and fails in production. Extend the existing comment block to say why.\n\n## Required tests (tasks 1.7, 1.8, 1.9)\n\nFollow `docs/testing.md`. These are Vitest unit tests in the `unit` project — no DB.\nAdd them to the existing test files; match their existing style.\n\n1.7 — valid iteration renders once per entry with fields substituted; and each of these\nfails boot **naming the construct**: undeclared item field, `each` over a scalar, over a\ngate-only path, over an unknown path, nested `each`, block params, `@index`, `@key`,\nhash argument on `each`, and a collection in value position.\n\n1.8 — sanitizer behavior end to end through the renderer: a `title` or `excerpt`\ncontaining the closing delimiter `</user_chat_history>` is escaped as content; a balanced\nforged copy of the reserved name (`<user_chat_history>...</user_chat_history>` inside a\nvalue) is escaped; exactly one delimiter pair survives in the rendered output. Also add\nthe direct `authored-text.test.ts` / `sanitize.test.ts` cases for the new reserved name.\n\n1.9 — against a **synthetic fixture template written inline in the test**, NOT the packaged\ndefault (which gains no digest block until layer 6): an owner with a digest but no\npersonalization leaves `{{#if user}}` false, so a personalization block and its framing\nprose are omitted while the digest renders.\n\nAlso cover the omission rules: empty collection omitted, `chats` omitted when both are\nempty, and the four-way boot probe rejecting the `{{#if user}}` + `{{#unless chats}}`\ntemplate.\n\n## Pass condition — all four must pass, run them yourself\n\n```bash\npnpm --filter api typecheck      # tsgo --noEmit\npnpm --filter api test           # vitest unit project\npnpm lint                        # oxlint --deny-warnings, all workspaces\npnpm --filter web test           # the web sanitize mirror has tests\n```\n\nThen format ONLY the files you touched:\n`pnpm exec prettier --write <each file you changed>`\nNever run a repo-wide format — it reformats unrelated files and creates review noise.\n\n## Conventions that will fail review if ignored\n\n- **`as unknown as T` is banned repo-wide** and enforced by a lefthook gate. Narrow the\n  dependency type instead — `apps/api/AGENTS.md` has the exact recipe with the shipped\n  `PromptUserResolver` exemplar.\n- Comments in this codebase explain **why**, not what, and are dense where a decision is\n  subtle. Match that register — the existing `prompt-loader.ts` comments are the model.\n  Do not strip or reflow existing comments.\n- Validation is **deny-by-default** and allowlist-based on purpose: it needs no revisiting\n  when handlebars adds a node kind. Do not convert anything to a blocklist.\n- Keep the diff minimal and scoped. No speculative abstraction, no unrequested config.\n\n## Final message\n\nReport: files changed, the four gate commands with their actual exit results, anything in\nthe spec you could not satisfy and why, and any place you judged the design underspecified.\nBe blunt about what you are unsure of — a hedge you flag is cheap, one you hide is not.\n",
