ution happens *outside* the binding transaction\n(there is a short separate read on the existing two-phase path in `chat-loop.service.ts`).\nThe setting value that **governs** is therefore the one observed **inside the binding\ntransaction**, not the one read while resolving. A candidate resolved under a setting value\nthat no longer holds at commit is **discarded rather than bound**, and the run proceeds\nwithout digest content rather than failing.\n\n### 5. Rendering the stored baseline (task 3.9)\n\nEvery run renders the **stored** baseline rather than re-querying, in `chat-loop.service.ts`\n**before hashing**, so `resolveEffectiveContext` addresses the snapshot by what was actually\nsent. Rendering must be deterministic: two runs of the same chat produce byte-identical\noutput and reuse the same snapshot instead of minting a new one.\n\nBecause layer 6 has not added the digest block to the packaged prompt, this renders to\nnothing today — that is expected and is exactly why this layer is not observable.\n\n### 6. Owner scoping — this is a tenant-isolation change\n\nRead only the requesting owner's chats, inside that owner's tenant scope\n(`TenantDbService.runAs`), with RLS as the enforcing boundary and application-level owner\nfilters retained as defense-in-depth. Unreachable through the public/shared-chat path, which\ncarries no owner identity. **Fail closed when identity is absent** — never open.\n\nDigest resolution or render failure must log the failure *kind* and **never a title or\nexcerpt** (task 3.14).\n\n`resolveAdvertisedTools` must receive no digest input at all — the advertised and executable\ntool set is identical with and without a digest, and task 3.15 asserts it.\n\n### 7. Summarization exclusion (task 3.18)\n\nExtend the summarization instruction in `apps/api/src/compaction/compaction.ts` to name the\ndigest delimiter (`<user_chat_history>`) alongside the personalization delimiter, in **both**\nthe full-current and transition instructions. The transition instruction is a separate code\npath; a regression there freezes other chats' excerpts into a permanent checkpoint. Do not\nalter the bound system prompt itself — the instruction is the request's final user message,\noutside the cached prefix.\n\n## Required tests (tasks 3.10-3.17)\n\nFollow `docs/testing.md`; `.integration.` infix = needs real Postgres. Every one of these is\nrequired, and several are the isolation proof for a tenancy change:\n\n- 3.10 unit: caps; disjointness with backfill to a full 10; exclusion rules; excerpt\n  truncation across scripts (include emoji/surrogate pairs and Cyrillic); byte-identical\n  renders across two runs of the same chat.\n- 3.11 integration: a second run in the same chat reuses the existing snapshot rather than\n  minting a new one.\n- 3.12 integration: one owner's digest never contains another owner's chats — with another\n  identity set, and with the empty identity.\n- 3.13 integration: the digest is absent on the public/shared-chat path and fails closed\n  when identity is absent.\n- 3.14: a resolution or render failure logs the failure kind and no title or excerpt.\n- 3.15: advertised and executable tool set identical with and without a resolved digest.\n- 3.16 integration: a chat whose first runs happened while the setting was off receives its\n  baseline on the first run after re-enabling, and emits no append before that baseline exists.\n- 3.17 integration: two concurrent initializing sends leave exactly one baseline epoch and no\n  divergent snapshots; a send whose binding transaction fails leaves no baseline behind.\n\n## Documentation (task 3.19)\n\nDocument the frozen-baseline lifecycle and its compaction re-bake in `apps/api/AGENTS.md`,\nplus the new migration in the migration-gotchas list if it needs any hand-appended statement.\n\n## Pass condition — all must pass, run them yourself\n\n```bash\npnpm --filter api typecheck\npnpm --filter api test\npnpm --filter api test:integration\npnpm lint\n```\n\n*