            "content": "---\nname: gh-stack-conflict-blocks-ci\ndescription: A gh-stack PR that conflicts with master gets NO pull_request workflow runs at all — silently, even though its own base is a clean fast-forward\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nOn a `gh stack` stack, a PR whose **cumulative** diff conflicts with **master** reports\n`mergeable: CONFLICTING / mergeStateStatus: DIRTY` even when its literal base branch is a\nstrict fast-forward — and GitHub then creates **zero** `pull_request` workflow runs for it.\nNo CI, no Lint, no error, no annotation. Sibling PRs in the same stack run normally.\n\nObserved 2026-08-13 on stack #337 (#307 recency digest): master gained 5 commits touching\nCHANGELOG.md/README.md; only the top layer (#354) edited those files, so only #354 went\nDIRTY and only #354 lost CI. `git merge-base` proved its base was a clean fast-forward, and\n`git merge-tree --write-tree origin/master <branch>` proved the real conflict was with master.\n\n**Why:** apparently mergeability for a stacked PR is evaluated against the stack's trunk, not\nits literal base. Not documented; inferred and then confirmed by the fix.\n\n**How to apply:**\n- Missing CI on exactly one stack PR → check `gh pr view N --json mergeable,mergeStateStatus`\n  FIRST. Do not chase it as a GitHub Actions hiccup.\n- These do **not** fix it and waste 10+ minutes each: close/reopen, `git commit --amend` +\n  force-push, `gh pr edit --base X` then back. All three were tried; all three left it DIRTY.\n- The fix is to rebase the stack onto current master (`gh stack sync`, or `gh stack rebase` +\n  `--continue` when sync aborts on conflicts). Mergeability flips to MERGEABLE and CI appears\n  within seconds.\n- `gh stack sync` cannot fast-forward local `master` if another worktree has it checked out\n  (see [[dev-server-placement]]) — it warns and rebases onto `origin/master` anyway, which is\n  fine.\n- Corollary: \"6 of 7 PRs are green\" is not evidence the 7th is fine. A PR with *no* checks\n  looks calmer than a red one. Count checks per PR, don't scan for red.\n\nRelated: [[pr-review-bot-timing]], [[llame-e2e-flaky-fails-ci]].\n",
